Build on musl: libc's msghdr (and cmsghdr) differ from glibc's.

On musl the libc crate's msghdr has private padding fields (__pad1, __pad2):
it cannot be written as a struct literal ("cannot construct `msghdr` with
struct literal syntax due to private fields"), and msg_iovlen is i32,
msg_controllen and cmsghdr.cmsg_len are u32 (glibc: usize). The msghdr is
now zeroed and its fields set with casts to the platform's types, and
cmsg_len is converted to usize.
Written for FenrirOS.

